{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/combinatorial-game-theory/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"why-cgt","title":"为何组合博弈论","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/combinatorial-game-theory/foundations/why-cgt","wordCount":1673,"readingTime":7},{"seq":2,"slug":"impartial-vs-partisan","title":"公平与党派游戏","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/combinatorial-game-theory/foundations/impartial-vs-partisan","wordCount":1280,"readingTime":6},{"seq":3,"slug":"game-model","title":"游戏与位置模型","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/combinatorial-game-theory/foundations/game-model","wordCount":1432,"readingTime":6}],"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"基础\">基础</h1><p>在真正动手判断&quot;谁必胜&quot;之前，需要先把研究对象立起来。这一章不解任何具体游戏，而是回答三个奠基性问题：这门学科为什么值得独立于经典博弈论存在、它研究的游戏该如何分类、以及&quot;一局游戏&quot;在数学上到底是什么。</p>\n<p>第一篇《为何组合博弈论》划定边界：它列出组合游戏的四条约束（双人、轮流、完全信息、无随机），解释为什么&quot;取走最后一子者胜&quot;这个看似琐碎的规则会催生一整套代数，并交代 Bouton、Conway、Berlekamp、Guy 这条历史脉络。第二篇《公平与党派游戏》给出全 hub 最重要的一条分类线：公平游戏（两方走法相同）与党派游戏（左右走法不同），并引入正常制与 misère 制的规则约定、以及 N/P（乃至党派游戏的四类）胜负归属。这条分类决定了后面你走公平游戏那条 Nim-Grundy 路线，还是党派游戏那条超现实数路线。</p>\n<p>第三篇《游戏与位置模型》是全 hub 的地基：把游戏递归地定义为 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>∣</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mi>R</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\{G^L \\mid G^R\\}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0913em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">{</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8413em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">L</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">∣</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0913em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8413em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0077em;\">R</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">}</span></span></span></span></span>——由左方的所有后继与右方的所有后继构成的集合，并说明位置、选项、游戏树/DAG、生日与等价的含义。之后无论是公平游戏的 Grundy 数，还是党派游戏的值，都是在这个模型上生长出来的。</p>\n<p>建议按 1→2→3 顺序读完本章再进入后续。读完你应当能做到：看到一个新游戏，立刻判断它是公平还是党派、用的是正常制还是 misère，并能把它的前几层位置画成一棵递归的游戏树。本章的分类会在 <a href=\"../impartial/\">公平</a> 与 <a href=\"../partisan/\">党派</a> 两章分别展开。</p>\n"}